{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions","id":156015,"title":"The membership numbers of the Traditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-01T15:28:44-07:00","id":156015,"title":"The membership numbers of the Traditions","content":"Not sure if the books actually went out and put this in approximate numbers or anything, but I was wondering how big or small individual Traditions membership are? <br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm talking about &quot;members&quot; as actually Awakened Mages not Sorcerer's or mundane followers and allies. <br /> <br /> All I really know right now from the top of my head is that apparently the Cult of Ecstasy is one the large Traditions on account of their methods of using foci, while the Euthanatos are much smaller, understandably so, because their paradigm sometimes requires you to kill people. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T16:12:47-07:00","id":156049,"title":"","content":"I did some digging on this very question a little while ago. I found somewhere Malcolm Shepperd, one of the free lancing writers/devs for M:tA in an archived post saying in HIS OPINION:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Waaaay too many Nephandi in that breakdown. To be Nephandus you have to enter the cauls, not just be bad. Plus, they have the smallest number of canonical NPCs. I'd put their numbers at less than 5%. There are also probably slightly fewer Orphans, since the Traditions really are pretty good at assimilating mystics. The Crafts have been beaten down by the Technocracy, to boot, but we'll be opstimistic with both. Plus, there are quite a lot of Technocrats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So I'd say:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Traditions- 40%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Technocracy- 40%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Marauders- 6%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Nephandi- 4%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Crafts- 10%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Orphans- 10%<br /> <br /> </span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Tytalus's note: Marauders and Nephandi are often &quot;part&quot; of another group first.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Canonically, the largest are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) OoH (they recruit more than any other Trad and the House structure lets them incorporate many different styles)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood (they recruit less than many Trads but have the largest population base to draw from).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">After that, the Dreamspeakers and Celestial Chorus are supposed to be pretty large and diverse. The Verbena trail slightly behind these two. The Ecstatics are probably about the size of the Verbena.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether are probably about equal size and next largest after the trads above.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Euthanatos are supposed to be smaller than the other Traditions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">To make some hard choices and put it all in a list, with breakdowns the ranking from largest to smallest would be:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Order of Hermes 15%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood 14%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3) Celestial Chorus 13%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4) Dreamspeakers 12%</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5) Verbena 11%*</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6) Cult of Ecstacy 11%*</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">7) Virtual Adepts 9%*</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">8) Sons of Ether 9%*</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">9) Euthanatos 6%</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">*The higher ranks Trad may have a fractionally higher number of members.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Bill Bridges revised the numbers during his run, which were originally 1 mage per million or 1 per 500,000, to 1 per 200,000 ro 250,000. Let's make it an even 30,000 Awakened mages in the world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That means the Traditions have 12,000 members.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Order of Hermes: 1800</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood: 1680</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3) Celestial Chorus: 1560</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4) Dreamspeakers: 1440</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5) Verbena: 1320</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6) Cult of Ecstacy: 1320</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">7) Virtual Adepts: 1080</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">8) Sons of Ether: 1080</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">9) Euthanatos: 720</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Breakdown by rank makes most Tradition mages Disciples, with a significant narrowing at Adept rank thanks to attrition and fewer apprentices because they tend to die more easily and because magic is generally in decline. So:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Apprentice 15% -- 1800 Traditionalists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Initiate: 20% -- 2400 Traditionalists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Disciple: 50% -- 6000 Traditionalists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Adept: 13% -- 1560 Traditionalists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Master: 1.9% -- 228 Traditionalists?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Archmaster: .1% 12 Traditionalists?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ranks will tend to break statistical predictions as the increase. For instance, thr Masters and archmasters are probably doled out more evenly that Tradition numbers would suggest. By contrast, the Technocracy probably has a fairly strict pyramidial distribution, with the fewest </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">on top and as many as half being &quot;Apprentices.&quot;</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 10-27-2019, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T16:20:10-07:00","id":156055,"title":"","content":"I think Malcom's numbers are decent as a baseline and can be dialed up or down as a Chronicle needs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:53:41-07:00","id":156128,"title":"","content":"I remember reading somewhere that Traditionalists outnumbered Technocrats. Is that no longer true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T22:50:18-07:00","id":156274,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=156128#post156128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading somewhere that Traditionalists outnumbered Technocrats. Is that no longer true?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some material to support that and I think Guide to the Technocracy says that the Technocracy also has thousands of &quot;extraordinary citizens&quot; and tens of thousands of mundane agents along with hundreds of thousands of people who fall under it's influence and serve it's needs in some capacity (from janitors to drivers).<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 31 of Sorcerer revised says the Union boasts hundreds of enlightened members as opposed to Malcolm's 12,000, that's a pretty big difference, (considering hundreds=less than two thousand).<br /> <br /> I believe Guide to The Traditions says there are thousands of tradition mages.<br /> <br /> Of course who gives a damn what Sorcerer revised and Guide to the Traditions/Technocracy say? The oWOD books contradict each other so much that half the hard facts you read contradict what it says in other books...<br /> <br /> The wisest of wise of whitewolf authors said &quot;this is because we want the lack of accurate information held by (put in splat type here) about other supernaturals to be clear, they don't know the real truth about each other and the inaccuracies in the books we publish reflect that, even when we're writing out of character and answering FAQs&quot;<br /> <br /> I personally like to make Tradition Mages more common than Enlightened Technocrats but don't normally allow mystical Sorcery in my modern Mage games where as I make Extraordinary Citizens common enough to outnumber the Tradition mages on their own.<br /> <br /> When I'm storytelling modern Mage games (post avatar storm in this case) I usually say there is one Trad Mage for every million people alive (7000 Trad mages roughly) and that there are about 10,000 mages involved in The Ascension war/on earth which means that there are about 3,000 technocrats and 1,000 others </span></span>(<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Craft Mages, Orphans Nephandi and Marauders)... that's if I even bother to consider hard number at all, which is usually just a waste of time anyways (for me) because it almost never comes into play in any meaningful way.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","user":"Dream_Walker","date":". 06-02-2014, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T23:24:37-07:00","id":157562,"title":"","content":"Wierdly enough in online games of a semi Mod variety the I've seen, majority of players that created character memberships listed Euthanatoi, Hermetics and Verbena as the most prominent populations of those Mage settings. It was also amusing to see that even on different online game chronicles the rivalry between Akashics and Euthanatoi may have been resolved, but animosity between the Euthanatoi and Hermetics was alive and well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T05:48:39-07:00","id":157747,"title":"","content":"Malcom's breakdown is very good, and his numbers can be scaled in any way you need or want. Here's what I do (basically):<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Bill Bridges revised the numbers during his run, which were originally 1 mage per million or 1 per 500,000, to 1 per 200,000 or 250,000.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> So depending on the city (or setting) and how thick you want the Mage-Blood to flow, you make this decision on your own and then calculate.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> Setting is San Francisco, which has about 4.5 million people to deal with.<br /> Say you want 10 mages in all of the metro area, you will have a density of 1 per 450,000 people.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind if this is a cross-over game, some of that population will be other supernaturals. That means you want a good idea of the total population of all of them combined as well. This is just a matter of tweaking the numbers until you get ratios you are happy with.<br /> <br /> Then you can use Malcom's breakdown with your chosen ratio, and filter that through your setting (NYC is a Mage hotbed, while Amarillo only has a single mage) to answer all your own questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 06-03-2014, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T23:14:11-08:00","id":769792,"title":"","content":"I'm bumping this thread because 1.) I think it's interesting and 2.) I think the context of not just the city, but beyond the number of Mages per city, the number of Mages per country becomes very interesting.<br /> <br /> Say we go with 1 in 200,000. Canada, then, at 35 million or so people, has 175 Mages. For the second largest country on the planet. That's pretty empty.<br /> <br /> Another point for the mathematically minded - is the long term effect of mages living a longer time. Yes, awakening is only weakly hereditary at best.. But living in Horizon Realms or the Umbra, or even just large Sanctums on Earth is a way for a mage to live far beyond a normal mortal life. I would think that the deaths from the ascension war might even that out however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T00:50:03-08:00","id":769807,"title":"","content":"I have this specific rule on number of Mages... (and Werewolves... and Vampires...) &quot;As Many as Plot needs&quot;.<br /> The whole census thing is entirely academic as you will never be able to mobilise and affect all these disparate individuals at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T03:07:50-08:00","id":769839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole census thing is entirely academic as you will never be able to mobilise and affect all these disparate individuals at once. </div> </div> </div>I agree it generally gets overplayed, but a setting with 10,000 magi is going to be radically different to one in which there are hundreds of thousands of them. Knowing what the original authors had in mind can be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T03:32:19-08:00","id":769844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=769792#post769792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say we go with 1 in 200,000. Canada, then, at 35 million or so people, has 175 Mages. For the second largest country on the planet. That's pretty empty.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By area, not by population. Going just by physical size is a poor way to justify a larger Awakened population, especially if there isn't a sizable Sleeper population to begin with. By your logic, Alaska should have the higher population of mages in the United States, but barely anyone lives there.<br /> <br /> Really, you should consider population density to assume Awakened population. More people=higher likelihood of mage presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T04:09:56-08:00","id":769855,"title":"","content":"The practical realities of roleplaying are more a determiner of local Mage populations than the real-world human population. Almost every story will have three-ish players, three or four Trad npcs, three or four Techno npcs, and a couple of Nephs. This is true whether the story is set in a small town, or a densely populated city. It's just the practical reality of storytelling necessities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:46:00-08:00","id":770038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=769844#post769844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By area, not by population. Going just by physical size is a poor way to justify a larger Awakened population, especially if there isn't a sizable Sleeper population to begin with. By your logic, Alaska should have the higher population of mages in the United States, but barely anyone lives there.<br /> <br /> Really, you should consider population density to assume Awakened population. More people=higher likelihood of mage presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood me - it wasn't an inditement of that calculation, just pointing out that the size of the Mage community in Canada would be very spread out and sparse, which is a different RPing environment than say, London or NY City. The ascension war in Canada (if it is being played) might look more like an elaborate game of chess vs NY where it's rebels vs MIB's.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cajunkan's point that the narrative will drive the # of mages more than a density calculation is quite valid IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T09:44:07-08:00","id":770075,"title":"","content":"A factor/facet of many Mage games/settings that is often overlooked -- and bears repeating -- is that when making numbers like those above (which are good, ball-park figures for general guesstimations) you need to keep in mind that *sorcerers/hedge-wizards/the numinically-blessed* comprise a very large proportion of the &quot;magic-using&quot; mortals of both the world, at large, as well as the Traditions themselves.<br /> <br /> From the Dark Ages to the Modern Era, for example, the OoH's roster of members has more (S)orcerers than (M)ages (that is, hedge-wizards vs. those who are fully Awakened) -- often in the ballpark of 3:1 (the &quot;lesser mages&quot; of the Order, who while useful are not part of the &quot;movers-and-shakers&quot;/leadership, proper, of the Tradition). A similar thing is true for the Verbena, the Akashics, any number of the CoE, the CC with its assorted True Faith healers/theurgists, and so on.<br /> <br /> This aspect is generally alluded to in a number of books (though only elaborated on, to a modest degree, in Sorcerer:Rev, proper), but narratively &quot;glossed over&quot; due to the focus on (M)ages in... well, Mage... which while thematically appropriate *does* tend to skew conceptual numbers when one is going about making lists like the ones above. It's an aspect that shouldn't be set aside when trying to get down to the nitty-gritty, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T10:07:38-08:00","id":770093,"title":"","content":"I am very confused by the numbers proposed in this thread. Why are Tradition numbers supposed to be on equal footing with those of the Technocracy? The number of mages should in my opinion align with the dominant paradigm. Mages are created from real people and don't (at least not with regularity) suddenly change their paradigm upon awakening. So if I had to break down percentages between TU, Trads and Crafts it would look more like this :<br /> <br /> Technocracy : 60%<br /> Trads : 30%<br /> Crafts (and Orphans) : 10%<br /> <br /> Nephandi are hard to count since they (in most cases) still feign allegiance to a certain faction and also depends heavily on the mood of the individual chronicle. The latter part also goes for Marauders.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions themselves I really don't see why the OoH would dominate in numbers. They have a very very rigid structure and HUGE demands upon their initiates. Hell they like to train their disciples to the point of awakening from the get go and dislike accepting people who awakened before they started training with them. How is that attitude going to produce the biggest Tradition? I see them (together with the Euthanatos) at the bottom as far as membership numbers go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:47:20-08:00","id":770304,"title":"","content":"If the dominant paradigm reinforces the ways of thinking that are not conductive to actual willworkers popping up, the dominant paradigm will not vastly outnumber the experimental rogue free spirits. Their suppport network and societal influence might, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T06:41:16-08:00","id":770693,"title":"","content":"A Scientific paradigm doesn't supress creativity. Quite the opposite in fact, thanks to technology things that would have seemed impossible a hundred years ago (or even just a mere 20) are now part of everyday life. So I really don't see why the dominant paradigm counteracts the awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T07:43:10-08:00","id":770726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Scientific paradigm doesn't supress creativity. </div> </div> </div>You haven't actually read the books then. You're not even wrong with that statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T08:27:57-08:00","id":770747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770726#post770726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You haven't actually read the books then. You're not even wrong with that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my biggest gripes about Mage BTW. Creativity is one of the core requirements of a good scientist, in the real world it takes an active and creative mind to find solutions to complex problems. In Mage however The Technocratic Paradigm kills creativity, which should mean nothing new or interesting gets discovered or made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9558-evildmmk3","name":"EvilDMMk3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T16:33:35-08:00","id":771046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilDMMk3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770747#post770747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of my biggest gripes about Mage BTW. Creativity is one of the core requirements of a good scientist, in the real world it takes an active and creative mind to find solutions to complex problems. In Mage however The Technocratic Paradigm kills creativity, which should mean nothing new or interesting gets discovered or made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creativity is dangerous. Until humanity is ready for it unbrideled creativity is just for the Technocrats. It's not that Technocracy wants to eradicate it, they just need their masses more pliable to get them ready for the big push.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:38:06-08:00","id":771215,"title":"","content":"I don't think the technocratic paradigm kills creativity at all. They just want creativity channeled into <i>constructive</i> endeavors. Tradition or Disparate magick and paradigms are not, however, considered constructive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:43:01-08:00","id":771218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770093#post770093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very confused by the numbers proposed in this thread. Why are Tradition numbers supposed to be on equal footing with those of the Technocracy? The number of mages should in my opinion align with the dominant paradigm. Mages are created from real people and don't (at least not with regularity) suddenly change their paradigm upon awakening. So if I had to break down percentages between TU, Trads and Crafts it would look more like this :<br /> <br /> Technocracy : 60%<br /> Trads : 30%<br /> Crafts (and Orphans) : 10%</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these numbers are way off - too many technocrats, not nearly enough traditionalists. Plus there are probably far more disparates than 10% of the total awakened population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:00:58-08:00","id":771346,"title":"","content":"I think the realistic ratios should be around<br /> 35% Technocrats<br /> 30% Traditionalists<br /> 25% Disparates<br /> 10% Marauders and Nephandi<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:08:38-08:00","id":771355,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like those percentages better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:21:26-08:00","id":771360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilDMMk3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770747#post770747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of my biggest gripes about Mage BTW. Creativity is one of the core requirements of a good scientist, in the real world it takes an active and creative mind to find solutions to complex problems. In Mage however The Technocratic Paradigm kills creativity, which should mean nothing new or interesting gets discovered or made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's what happens when you fully equal Technocracy to science, but the books agree that's not quite true either. The Technocracy has a lot of baggages behind after all. There is definitely creativity behind science (and Mage makes that clear a lot of times around the line) the same as in the rest of magick, because magick is active by definition. The problem is who is behind it, something that applies to all mages, not just the Union.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:54:11-08:00","id":771784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=769807#post769807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this specific rule on number of Mages... (and Werewolves... and Vampires...) &quot;As Many as Plot needs&quot;.<br /> The whole census thing is entirely academic as you will never be able to mobilise and affect all these disparate individuals at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Line 1 YES!<br /> Line 2 NO!<br /> <br /> It's not academic and having a firm understanding is DAMN IMPORTANT for many storytellers, they need a hard number to think properly and that's crucial to running a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:55:47-08:00","id":771788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=156274#post156274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><br /> <br /> There's some material to support that and I think Guide to the Technocracy says that the Technocracy also has thousands of &quot;extraordinary citizens&quot; and tens of thousands of mundane agents along with hundreds of thousands of people who fall under it's influence and serve it's needs in some capacity (from janitors to drivers).<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 31 of Sorcerer revised says the Union boasts hundreds of enlightened members as opposed to Malcolm's 12,000, that's a pretty big difference, (considering hundreds=less than two thousand).<br /> <br /> I believe Guide to The Traditions says there are thousands of tradition mages.<br /> <br /> Of course who gives a damn what Sorcerer revised and Guide to the Traditions/Technocracy say? The oWOD books contradict each other so much that half the hard facts you read contradict what it says in other books...<br /> <br /> The wisest of wise of whitewolf authors said &quot;this is because we want the lack of accurate information held by (put in splat type here) about other supernaturals to be clear, they don't know the real truth about each other and the inaccuracies in the books we publish reflect that, even when we're writing out of character and answering FAQs&quot;<br /> <br /> I personally like to make Tradition Mages more common than Enlightened Technocrats but don't normally allow mystical Sorcery in my modern Mage games where as I make Extraordinary Citizens common enough to outnumber the Tradition mages on their own.<br /> <br /> When I'm storytelling modern Mage games (post avatar storm in this case) I usually say there is one Trad Mage for every million people alive (7000 Trad mages roughly) and that there are about 10,000 mages involved in The Ascension war/on earth which means that there are about 3,000 technocrats and 1,000 others </span></span>(<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Craft Mages, Orphans Nephandi and Marauders)... that's if I even bother to consider hard number at all, which is usually just a waste of time anyways (for me) because it almost never comes into play in any meaningful way.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is confirmed with regards to the statement about the numbers in Sorcerer Revised and Guide to the Traditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:58:40-08:00","id":771793,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer using the model dream walker proposed, the technocracy is too oppressive to be the larger body (I know someone will think of a great reason to disagree but I feel the way I feel) and I like the idea that the Trads have more mages but that the Union has so many extraordinary citizens that it can use that leverage.<br /> <br /> Also Malcolm Shepherds numbers are just plain WRONG, they add up to 110%!!!<br /> <br /> HOW DID ALL THE PEOPLE GOING &quot;YA GOOD NUMBERS&quot; NOT NOTICE THAT!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:44:36-08:00","id":772123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=771784#post771784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Line 1 YES!<br /> Line 2 NO!<br /> <br /> It's not academic and having a firm understanding is DAMN IMPORTANT for many storytellers, they need a hard number to think properly and that's crucial to running a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's absolutley irrelevant. You need as many Mages you need to staff your story, all the other Mages in the setting do not even exist. Heck a game where the Technocracy rules the world and the characters fight under the heel of Big Brother is a different world from one in which they both coexist in a world very similar to ours or the world where the Technocracy are the underdogs with few mages but many resoources, or a world where the traditions are almost extinct.<br /> <br /> If you actually consider how different the games we all run with Mage are you'll see how nebulous an exact census is. The number of mages is something that's entirely dependant on the tone and style of the game you're running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 11-23-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:54:50-08:00","id":772128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=771793#post771793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOW DID ALL THE PEOPLE GOING &quot;YA GOOD NUMBERS&quot; NOT NOTICE THAT!!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>To pipe in here for a moment, because people were more looking at and agreeing with the general relationships between the numbers, than the total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T03:42:52-08:00","id":772202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770693#post770693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scientific paradigm doesn't supress creativity. Quite the opposite in fact, thanks to technology things that would have seemed impossible a hundred years ago (or even just a mere 20) are now part of everyday life. So I really don't see why the dominant paradigm counteracts the awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether it suppresses creativity isn't the point. If you have one unified paradigm, there is going to be less variation of practice, and less need for a lot of willworkers to support and explore its permutations. That there are fewer Enlightened Technocrats than Awakened Traditionalists speaks to the former's success--their control of the paradigm makes them more efficient. It allows them to delegate a lot of their work to Extraordinary Citizens and even more ordinary citizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T05:18:28-08:00","id":772238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=770726#post770726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A Scientific paradigm doesn't supress creativity.&quot;<br /> <br /> You haven't actually read the books then. You're not even wrong with that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/8/7058/6893257321_c7aa61307b_b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>A Scientific paradigm doesn't suppress creativity.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:56:09-08:00","id":772408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=772202#post772202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It allows them to delegate a lot of their work to Extraordinary Citizens and even more ordinary citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, put another way, so many ritual bonus successes omnomnom.<br /> <br /> This is the true power of the Technoparadigm (yes, including SoE and VA groups that use commonly-practiced science), that they can take Microsoft or IBM or NIMH or some other large concentration of trained professionals, one single Enlightened person with the right Spheres, and churn out huge Consensual Effects on a reasonably regular basis.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly, the hugeness of Paradox Backlashes from botching is problematic, since you sometimes get massive institutional failures, missed deadlines, and Windows ME.)<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes could've had this as well, but sadly they dropped the ball on the &quot;teach our magic to everybody so that we can reap the benefits of <i>so many ritual assistants everywhere</i>&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:20:19-08:00","id":793136,"title":"","content":"I know this isn't exactly the topic at hand, but this annoys me a lot.<br /> <br /> While I love using conservative numbers for the supernatural beings in my chronicles, such as 1 mage for 250 thousand people, because this provokes more political bickering, territorialism and reasons for the players to unite in a group; I have to agree with the guy who gave the example of Canada, that this also creates some strange asymmetries.<br /> A country like Switzerland, Israel or Austria, averaging a population of 8 million, would have... 32 mages at best. You either have supernatural beings concentrated in megalopoli like New York, Shanghai and Moscow or you have them occupying a huge sparse area, completely isolated from each other, like feudal dukes.<br /> <br /> I can see this making sense with vampires, 90% of their after lives are dedicated to securing food source and engaging in political confrontations; they also don't have mobility because of the sun.<br /> But mages? It feel incoherent and I always need to fill my chronicles with side characters, crafts, sorcerers and hedge wizards, which lead the mages to act more as a privileged elite, as enlightened despots, than... Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:03:10-08:00","id":793222,"title":"","content":"What is helpful is to do two things. One of which you're doing. Just like in Mage the Awakening and the Orders/Ministires the bulk of the Traditions/Technocracy is made up of sleepwalkers, sorcerer, psi, hedge magic (minor template) types and even sleepers in certain public positions where magic isn't practiced.<br /> <br /> The other thing that you realize is that mages gather in concentrations are magic phenomena/mystery/resources. They don't really follow the exact population in a given geographic area or location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:15:40-08:00","id":793305,"title":"","content":"I tend to use fairly heavy numbers on the Mage front, oftentimes on the 1:50k or even sometimes as many as 1:10k, but I offset this by having the vast bulk of them as low-Arete Orphans with the Sleepwalker flaw who use low-mysticism Instruments: genius martial artists, top of the line hackers, brilliant chemists and other individuals who exist in that blurred space between 'highly competent' and 'superhuman'. It also provides a handy talent pool for the various groups to fight over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":". 12-26-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:48:47-08:00","id":793644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=793222#post793222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really follow the exact population in a given geographic area or location.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly why I feel uncomfortable with the relation of mage:human population being dictated by quantity.<br /> While Vampires have reasons to be more numerous where there is more food for them, that is, crowded cities, there is nothing implying that there are more mages in India or China simply because China and India have huge populations; I don't see any reason why there are 626 mages in Bangladesh and only 32 in Switzerland.<br /> I suppose mage population and population density should be according to quintessence sources.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:00:39-08:00","id":793682,"title":"","content":"Just for fun, these are the official population of mages that every house of Hermes have in Ars Magica setting:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bonisagus: 81 mages (52 Bonisagi, 29 Trianomae);</li> <li>Quaesitor: 98 (plus 41 non Guernitus Quaesitor);</li> <li>Flambeau: 114 (19 in Proven\u00e7al Tribunal);</li> <li>Tytalus: 96;</li> <li>Verditius: 74;</li> <li>Ex Micellanea: estimated 180 mages;</li> <li>Mercere: 150 (12 &quot;awakened&quot;);</li> <li>Tremere: 92 (41 in Transylvania);</li> <li>Jerbition: 102 (26 in Tribunal of the Great Alps);</li> <li>Bjomaer: 79;</li> <li>Merinita: 68;</li> <li>Criamon: 94;</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:35:31-08:00","id":793836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=793682#post793682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, these are the official population of mages that every house of Hermes have in Ars Magica setting: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bonisagus: 81 mages (52 Bonisagi, 29 Trianomae);</li> <li>Quaesitor: 98 (plus 41 non Guernitus Quaesitor);</li> <li>Flambeau: 114 (19 in Proven\u00e7al Tribunal);</li> <li>Tytalus: 96;</li> <li>Verditius: 74;</li> <li>Ex Micellanea: estimated 180 mages;</li> <li>Mercere: 150 (12 &quot;awakened&quot;);</li> <li>Tremere: 92 (41 in Transylvania);</li> <li>Jerbition: 102 (26 in Tribunal of the Great Alps);</li> <li>Bjomaer: 79;</li> <li>Merinita: 68;</li> <li>Criamon: 94;</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>So when we have around 65 million of people in Europe the 1200s there is 1228 Mages just in the Order of Hermes. The Messianic Voices, the Ahl-I-Batin, Spirit Talkers are probably similar in size while the Valderman are smaller. That puts the global number of mages quite high at a time when there is vastly less humans than today.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T23:05:59-08:00","id":794636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=772408#post772408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, put another way, so many ritual bonus successes omnomnom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely part of it. More than that though, the Technocracy doesn't have to do as much actual magic, because their paradigm is so dominant and they have a lot of institutional power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:11:03-08:00","id":829561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=772128#post772128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To pipe in here for a moment, because people were more looking at and agreeing with the general relationships between the numbers, than the total.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough, good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:13:16-08:00","id":829563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=772123#post772123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's absolutley irrelevant. You need as many Mages you need to staff your story, all the other Mages in the setting do not even exist. Heck a game where the Technocracy rules the world and the characters fight under the heel of Big Brother is a different world from one in which they both coexist in a world very similar to ours or the world where the Technocracy are the underdogs with few mages but many resoources, or a world where the traditions are almost extinct.<br /> <br /> If you actually consider how different the games we all run with Mage are you'll see how nebulous an exact census is. The number of mages is something that's entirely dependant on the tone and style of the game you're running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok pal, whatever you say, we're all different and all have different needs is the only thing not worth chopping out of your post, and you've even missed that.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone else needs the numbers to feel comfortable running the game in first place and maybe they'll run a better game than you ever will even though they need something you apparently don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T06:16:54-08:00","id":829686,"title":"","content":"But you shouldn't forget the human population in some Horizon realms. Maybe there are parallel earths, or planets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T09:09:19-07:00","id":1119904,"title":"","content":"I always liked having the Technocracy be smaller in terms of actual Enlightened members, with the bulk of the scientific and military might coming from clones, semi-Enlightened Citizens, HIT Marks, and the like. Gives them more hitting power and makes the Enlightened feel like an elite.<br /> I never got a lot of use out of Sorcerers (mainly because I never bought the book). Anyone have more info on how they work in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T01:06:48-07:00","id":1124218,"title":"","content":"I generally like the percentage breakdowns presented in this thread, but have some issues that I would like to raise for discussion. <br /> <br /> Firstly, I have a query about numbers relating to Crafts that are clearly rooted in a specific culture pertaining to an ethnic group. In this instance, I'm thinking of the Kopa Loei. (1) There are currently just under 700k people in the entirety of Polynesia (irrespective of ethnicity). (2) With 1 Mage/250k people, there might be 3 awakened, total, in this entire group of islands. (Yes, I'm aware that there are plenty of Polynesian background people living outside the islands. Even if we said the equivalent population was outside the islands, it'd only be 6 awakened.) 3) M20 indicates that a typical Kopa Loei group is between 2-20 members.<br /> <br /> Are there just more Kopa Loei as a percentage of the population of Polynesia? Alternatively, are there a disproportionate number of people outside &quot;Polynesian&quot; culture (I balk at this term, as Maori culture is quite distinct from Hawaiian or Samoan or Tahitian and so on) that are Kopa Loei? If so...isn't this cultural appropriation? As a person living in the Pacific Rim, the grouping of all these different cultural group under one &quot;Craft&quot; is only slightly better than the original &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Next, I'm skeptical about the OoH having the highest percentage of Mages, particularly in contrast to traditions like the VA. What's the justification for these percentage splits? I'd have thought that VA would be on the up, particularly considering the pervasiveness of the Web (since Revised came out). I think it might be good to revisit these percentages, and also indicate which way the trend is with regards to numbers. That is, which traditions are increasing in membership, and which are not. <br /> <br /> Finally, separately, can someone please explain why the Wu Lung are experiencing reduced numbers (M20) to the extent that they've relaxed their &quot;all-male&quot; and &quot;Han Chinese&quot; standard? Surely in mainland China, with a population of 1.4 billion will have at least a few Wu Leng? That gives us 5400 awakened in China...even if only 1% are Wu Leng, that's still 54 purely in mainland China. I'd hazard there'd be a few more....<br /> <br /> TL;DR Newbie posts long-winded remark about global demographics, ethnicity and sects as first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:53:01-07:00","id":1124814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cerulean Scream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=1124218#post1124218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally like the percentage breakdowns presented in this thread, but have some issues that I would like to raise for discussion.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I have a query about numbers relating to Crafts that are clearly rooted in a specific culture pertaining to an ethnic group. In this instance, I'm thinking of the Kopa Loei. (1) There are currently just under 700k people in the entirety of Polynesia (irrespective of ethnicity). (2) With 1 Mage/250k people, there might be 3 awakened, total, in this entire group of islands. (Yes, I'm aware that there are plenty of Polynesian background people living outside the islands. Even if we said the equivalent population was outside the islands, it'd only be 6 awakened.) 3) M20 indicates that a typical Kopa Loei group is between 2-20 members.<br /> <br /> Are there just more Kopa Loei as a percentage of the population of Polynesia? Alternatively, are there a disproportionate number of people outside &quot;Polynesian&quot; culture (I balk at this term, as Maori culture is quite distinct from Hawaiian or Samoan or Tahitian and so on) that are Kopa Loei? If so...isn't this cultural appropriation? As a person living in the Pacific Rim, the grouping of all these different cultural group under one &quot;Craft&quot; is only slightly better than the original &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Next, I'm skeptical about the OoH having the highest percentage of Mages, particularly in contrast to traditions like the VA. What's the justification for these percentage splits? I'd have thought that VA would be on the up, particularly considering the pervasiveness of the Web (since Revised came out). I think it might be good to revisit these percentages, and also indicate which way the trend is with regards to numbers. That is, which traditions are increasing in membership, and which are not.<br /> <br /> Finally, separately, can someone please explain why the Wu Lung are experiencing reduced numbers (M20) to the extent that they've relaxed their &quot;all-male&quot; and &quot;Han Chinese&quot; standard? Surely in mainland China, with a population of 1.4 billion will have at least a few Wu Leng? That gives us 5400 awakened in China...even if only 1% are Wu Leng, that's still 54 purely in mainland China. I'd hazard there'd be a few more....<br /> <br /> TL;DR Newbie posts long-winded remark about global demographics, ethnicity and sects as first post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is exactly the problem one has the minute you say &quot;1:10,000&quot; anything. It's a general rubric that works say, for how many mages or vampires are in New York City, and completely falls apart the minute you try and apply it to a country like Canada, or in your example, Polynesia. You could say there are a couple willworkers on every island, of varying powers, and leave it at that. <br /> <br /> The OoH is given the highest % because of their in canon programs to literally force bright mortals to awaken through sheer force of will. The VA's are drawn from computer nerds typically, and have been a very slight minority of the population only up until the last 15 years or so. <br /> <br /> The more you try and figure out the number, the more the setting doesn't seem to make sense. Don't look to hard. Figure out some appropriate Mind Caulk and move on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:53:13-07:00","id":1124859,"title":"","content":"I must be missing something from early on in this discussion. Malcolms numbers don't add up correctly. <br /> <br /> &quot;Traditions- 40%<br /> Technocracy- 40%<br /> Marauders- 6%<br /> Nephandi- 4%<br /> Crafts- 10%<br /> Orphans- 10%&quot;<br /> <br /> That's 110%...<br /> <br /> The rest seem fine however.<br /> <br /> Edit: ah it seems that was caught on the second page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:58:00-07:00","id":1125095,"title":"","content":"Uhm...the Traditions should grossly outnumber the Technocracy. Or are we assuming religion is less believed in the World of Darkness? One might think people would pray harder there. I felt the Technocracy's primary advantage was never numbers but UNITY. Also, the fact it uses the wealth of corporations and governments to bolster it's power plus legions of magically created slaves along with acolytes.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I go do my own numbers for mages with a significant role for Hedge Mages.<br /> <br /> In my games, they outnumber the True Mages by a factor of 5/1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-05-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T12:22:22-07:00","id":1125304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhm...the Traditions should grossly outnumber the Technocracy. Or are we assuming religion is less believed in the World of Darkness? One might think people would pray harder there. I felt the Technocracy's primary advantage was never numbers but UNITY. Also, the fact it uses the wealth of corporations and governments to bolster it's power plus legions of magically created slaves along with acolytes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always interesting to remember that.<br /> <br /> One thing that hasn't been given a lot of atention in Mage it's the requiting practices of the different Factions. I think that it's very important, religious people that awaken aren't automatically members of the Traditions (and I imagine that orthodox and fanatics may not be fond of the syncretism of the Chorus, nor of working with witches/pagans). There should be some explaining on how the Traditions manage to convince so many people.<br /> <br /> I imagine the mind of the recently awakened it's more pliable, and that a judicious use of magic may make easier to locate them, but this aspect of the game lacks exploration. Actually, the Dreamspeakers have an interesting method: Some spirits know this tradition to be &quot;spirit friendly&quot;, and thus when they find orphans that have a connection with the spirit world, they may try to guide them into the Tradition.<br /> <br /> Also, the violent recruiting methods of the Technocracy, that includes bribe, capture and brainwashing, may account for their numbers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:19:15-07:00","id":1125324,"title":"","content":"The Syndicate convention book has several examples of mages who play along because they are in debt, fiscal or otherwise, to groups controlled by Syndicate members. Also, I'm sure that Technocracy is happy to convert Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts back to Union members if the effort is not too high.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T15:59:24-07:00","id":1125717,"title":"","content":"Celestial Chorusters or Orphans who are Celestial Chorus-ish should be the majority of Mages. America is 95% Christian, and third world countries will mostly be just as high. Celestial Chorusters(or Celestial Chorus-ish orphans) should completely dwarf Hermetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T16:18:34-07:00","id":1125727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=1125717#post1125717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> America is 95% Christian, and third world countries will mostly be just as high.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given the number of church closing and parish consolation I really doubt that. Isn't the catholic church having a problem finding priests? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T17:11:02-07:00","id":1125731,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay, I did get the numbers wrong: just under 71 percent of Americans are Christian, with other religious groups adding up to another 6 percent. Worldwide 84 percent of people are religious. That's still crushingly more than the number of people who take Hermeticism seriously. The Celestial Chorus should dominate every area dominated by an Abrahamic religion. Hinduism I'm not sure whether that would produce more CC's, Akash's, or Euth's, but it sure wouldn't produce a lot of Herm's.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T17:50:03-07:00","id":1125741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions?p=1125731#post1125731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, okay, I did get the numbers wrong: just under 71 percent of Americans are Christian, with other religious groups adding up to another 6 percent. Worldwide 84 percent of people are religious. That's still crushingly more than the number of people who take Hermeticism seriously. The Celestial Chorus should dominate every area dominated by an Abrahamic religion. Hinduism I'm not sure whether that would produce more CC's, Akash's, or Euth's, but it sure wouldn't produce a lot of Herm's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found data from Gallup and Pew Research Center which conflict with one another. I also question the validity of any such figure due to it largely being guesswork based on poll data. Since the US government would never include such information in a census we'll not have a true figure. One must also keep in mind that the Celestial Chorus is not an Abrahamic religion at all, even if some of their beliefs are similar, so the religion of sleepers won't really have an impact on their numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T18:24:07-07:00","id":1125750,"title":"","content":"I disagree. The preponderance of Abrahamic religions would either create CCers, or even more likely, orphans who are CCish, even if they aren't exactly CCers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:38:23-07:00","id":1125935,"title":"","content":"But there are Christians and there are *Christians* who are pious, devout and *believe*. The former outweigh the latter by a wide margin. Remember, this is the WoD, and many of the Traditions go back a long time and have various levels of infrastrcture. There is nothing saying that Christians are not in the other Traditions. As well, a very salient point on World Building: Most of the original developers for Mage were not Christians, nor were raised in the Bible Belt - *I think*. This would have a huge effect on how they perceive the effects of Religion in their world.<br /> <br /> In DA Mage for example, it's strongly hinted that the Messianics (old name for the Celestial Chorus) are the dominant faction by a mile. But the Ascension War split them into chunks and Many in the early Order of Reason were Christians as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}